# ── Source data (read-only inputs, ~1.3 GB) ────────────────────────────────
# These are the original, read-only source collections the dataset is built
# from. They are third-party data, not project code, and together they are
# ~1.3 GB - well past what a Git repository should carry (GitHub warns above
# 1 GB and discourages files over 50 MB). They are also not reproducible from
# this repo, so committing them would help nobody.
#
# To version them anyway, use Git LFS rather than deleting these lines:
#   git lfs install
#   git lfs track "Balanced_Final_Split/**/*.jpg" "Irrelevant/**/*"
Balanced_Final_Split/
Irrelevant/

# ── Project artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The generated dataset is 5,929 JPEGs (~1 GB). Rebuild it with
# `python grape.py --build-dataset` rather than committing a gigabyte of images.
#
# The reports and figures under results/ ARE committed: they are the evidence
# behind the accuracy claimed in README.md, and they are only 4.4 MB.
Balanced_From_Sources/train/
Balanced_From_Sources/test/
Balanced_From_Sources/results/split_manifest.csv

# Trained weights (89 MB). Regenerate with `python grape.py`, or distribute
# best_iwnet.pth out of band (GitHub Releases, LFS) - not through git history.
*.pth
*.pt

# ── Local configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
config.local.yaml

# ── Editors / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
